    "done_when": "docs/evidence/fragments/jt60sa-machine-map/jtmm-mast-pin-drift.html explains, read-only, why tests/gs/test_artifact_resolution.py::test_re_authoring_reproduces_the_identity_the_package_pins fails on main. Re-authoring now yields semantic identity sha256:f20d64dbde63756150fecd5a41d34a0d7a055900877370aae40a594ca7d039d5, while imas_ambix/gs/artifact_resolution.py PINNED_DESCRIPTIONS pins MAST at sha256:8df7a0a6c3f6162dbe0f226660bc069f37de8eb69f0f7c80bbfedc2bd4be220c. Author MAST's description afresh with author_pinned_description('mast') into a cache directory under the run directory, never ~/.cache. Read the pinned artifact's manifest from ~/.cache/imas-ambix/machine-artifact, read-only, for example the object sha256:16cb20357da22dac498813c7953c380871e3429648f793d6c87aad6c09937ebc the failing test resolved. Compare the two manifests field by field over every field the semantic identity covers: the dictionary pin, the physical and registry digests, the shot ranges, completeness and gaps, the field evidence and the channel drives. Name each field that differs, quoting both values or their first differing entries. Then name the nova commit that changed it, by reading git -C /home/ITER/mcintos/Code/nova log over nova/imas and nova/catalog since the pin was recorded. aff62b24 and 28a8247b on 2026-10-08 are the first suspects, and you confirm or rule them out from their diffs. Close with a recommendation: repin MAST if the change is an intended change to the description's content, or name the nova regression and the nova file and line to fix if the identity changed without the description changing. Nothing in nova, maps/ or ~/.cache is written. Run on the fleet allocation (SLURM_JOB_ID set).",
